index 28b0891..f93af02 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -26,19 +26,35 @@ BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle update --conservative fizzy-saas
 
 ## Working with Stripe
 
-The first time, you need to:
+Run the SaaS database migrations with `bin/rails db:migrate:saas` in SaaS mode.
 
-1. Install Stripe CLI: https://stripe.com/docs/stripe-cli
-2. Run `stripe login` and authorize the environment `37signals Development`
+In the Stripe environment for this deployment, configure two recurring USD monthly prices:
 
-Then, for working on the Stripe integration locally, you need to run this script to start the tunneling and set the environment variables:
+| Plan | Price | Storage | Price ID environment variable |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
+| Free (1,000 published cards) | Free | 1 GB | Not used |
+| Unlimited | $20/month | 5 GB | `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` |
+| Unlimited+ | $25/month | 500 GB | `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID` |
+
+Set `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` to an API key for that environment. Configure Stripe Checkout to limit customers to one subscription. Enable payment method updates, cancellation, and switching between both prices in Stripe’s customer portal configuration. Recurring billing is canceled from the portal, not by deleting the Fizzy account.
+If overriding `CSP_FORM_ACTION`, include `https://checkout.stripe.com` and `https://billing.stripe.com` so browsers can follow redirects from billing forms.
+
+Add `POST /stripe/webhooks` (with no account slug) as a Stripe webhook destination for `customer.subscription.created`, `.updated`, `.deleted`, `.paused`, and `.resumed`. Set `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` to that endpoint’s signing secret. Fizzy reads the customer’s current subscriptions from Stripe when it receives one of these events; an active, trialing, or past-due subscription on a configured price grants its plan. A canceled or unpaid subscription does not grant a paid plan.
+
+To try checkout and the portal locally, set both test-mode price IDs and the test API key, then run:
+
+```sh
+stripe login
+stripe listen --forward-to http://localhost:3000/stripe/webhooks
+```
+
+Export the signing secret printed by `stripe listen` as `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` before starting `bin/dev`. The automated billing tests don’t contact Stripe:
 
 ```sh
-eval "$(BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle exec stripe-dev)"
-bin/dev # You need to start the dev server in the same terminal session
+SAAS=1 DATABASE_ADAPTER=sqlite bin/rails test saas/test/integration/hosted_billing_test.rb saas/test/controllers/stripe_webhooks_controller_test.rb saas/test/controllers/account/billing_test.rb
 ```
 
-This will ask for your 1password authorization to read and set the environment variables that Stripe needs.
+Staff can manage comps and usage overrides at `/admin/accounts`. A comp grants Unlimited without starting or canceling a Stripe subscription; an account already subscribed to Unlimited+ keeps its higher allowance. Resetting a usage override restores measured usage.
 
 ### Stripe environments
 
diff --git a/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb b/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb
